      },
      "message": "perf(sim): a field block stock builds in closed form, not by band fill\n\n#633: the field engine took ~58 s (release) to BUILD a 120 mm block at\na 0.375 mm cell - the floorless block is meshed ten spans deep and the\nBFS band fill sampled every cell along those walls - while its cuts\ntook milliseconds. A block's mesh-layer magnitude is now the box's\nexact closed-form distance (field_box::AnalyticBox): SdfField::from_box\nstores no bricks and mag_at answers unstored cells from the box,\nclamped to cap. Build: 58 s -> 42 us; same cut cells (399/416).\n\nPinned by field_block_cost: a block stores no band at build; the\nclosed form reads the band-filled stock's sign everywhere within two\ncells; a heavy-lane budget (120 mm block + drill under 2 s, release).\n\nFixes #633\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
